 2001} \\left\\lfloor \\frac{4050}{m} \\right\\rfloor\\).\n\nCombining these, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\sum_{m=-1999, \\text{ step } 2}^{2001} \\left\\lfloor \\frac{4050}{m} \\right\\rfloor = -\\sum_{m \\text{ odd}, 1 \\leq m \\leq 1999} \\left\\lceil \\frac{4050}{m} \\right\\rceil + \\sum_{m \\text{ odd}, 1 \\leq m \\leq 2001} \\left\\lfloor \\frac{4050}{m} \\right\\rfloor\n\\]\n\nWe rewrite the positive sum as:\n\n\\[\n\\sum_{m \\text{ odd}, 1 \\leq m \\leq 2001} \\left\\lfloor \\frac{4050}{m} \\right\\rfloor = \\sum_{m \\text{ odd}, 1 \\leq m \\leq 1999} \\left\\lfloor \\frac{4050}{m} \\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor \\frac{4050}{2001} \\right\\rfloor\n\\]\n\nThus, the total sum becomes:\n\n\\[\n-\\sum_{m \\text{ odd}, 1 \\leq m \\leq 1999} \\left\\lceil \\frac{4050}{m} \\right\\rceil + \\sum_{m \\text{ odd}, 1 \\leq m \\leq 1999} \\left\\lfloor \\frac{4050}{m} \\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor \\frac{4050}{2001} \\right\\rfloor\n\\]\n\nThe difference between the sums over \\(\\left\\lfloor \\frac{4050}{m} \\right\\rfloor\\) and \\(\\left\\lceil \\frac{4050}{m} \\right\\rceil\\) for \\(1 \\leq m \\leq 1999\\) is \\(-1\\) for non-integer values and \\(0\\) for integer values. The number of integer values where \\(\\frac{4050}{m}\\) is an integer is the number of odd divisors of \\(4050\\) up to \\(1999\\). The odd divisors of \\(4050\\) are the divisors of \\(2025\\) (since \\(4050 = 2 \\times 2025\\)), which are \\(1, 3, 5, 9, 15, 25, 27, 45, 75, 81, 135, 225, 405, 675, 2025\\). Excluding \\(2025\\), there are \\(14\\) such divisors.\n\nThus, the difference sum is \\(- (1000 - 14) = -986\\). Adding the remaining term \\(\\left\\lfloor \\frac{4050}{2001} \\right\\rfloor = 2\\):\n\n\\[\n-986 + 2 = -984\n\\]\n\nThe final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-984}\n\\]","num_tokens":17397,"correct":true,"formatted":true}],"avg_output_tokens":20094.5,"num_correct":8,"pass_at_gen_n":true,"majority_vote_correct":true,"predicted_answer":"-984","full_generation":" Okay, so I have this probl