\nS_15 = 5953/16384 + 1/32768 = (11906 + 1)/32768 = 11907/32768 ≈0.363372802734375\n\nS_16 = 11907/32768 + 1/65536 = (23814 + 1)/65536 = 23815/65536 ≈0.3633880615234375\n\nS_17 = 23815/65536 - 1/131072 = (47630 - 1)/131072 = 47629/131072 ≈0.36338043212890625\n\nS_18 = 47629/131072 + ... but let's see if there's a pattern in the fractions.\n\nLooking at the numerators and denominators:\n\nS_1 = 1/2\n\nS_2 = 1/4\n\nS_3 = 3/8\n\nS_4 = 5/16\n\nS_5 = 11/32\n\nS_6 = 23/64\n\nS_7 = 47/128\n\nS_8 = 95/256\n\nS_9 = 187/512\n\nS_10 = 373/1024\n\nS_11 = 745/2048\n\nS_12 = 1489/4096\n\nS_13 = 2977/8192\n\nS_14 = 5953/16384\n\nS_15 = 11907/32768\n\nS_16 = 23815/65536\n\nS_17 = 47629/131072\n\nHmm, I notice that each numerator seems to be roughly doubling and adding or subtracting 1:\n\nLooking at the numerators:\n\nStarting from S_1 numerator: 1\n\nS_2: 1\n\nWait S_1: 1/2 → numerator 1\n\nS_2: 1/4 → numerator 1\n\nWait, but S_3 is 3/8. Hmm, let's see:\n\nWait S_1 = 1/2 → numerator 1, denominator 2\n\nS_2 = 1/4 → numerator 1, denominator 4\n\nS_3 = 3/8 → numerator 3, denominator 8\n\nS_4 = 5/16 → numerator 5, denominator 16\n\nS_5 = 11/32 → numerator 11, denominator 32\n\nS_6 = 23/64 → numerator 23, denominator 64\n\nS_7 = 47/128 → numerator 47, denominator 128\n\nS_8 = 95/256 → numerator 95, denominator 256\n\nS_9 = 187/512 → numerator 187, denominator 512\n\nS_10 = 373/1024 → numerator 373, denominator 1024\n\nS_11 = 745/2048 → numerator 745, denominator 2048\n\nS_12 = 1489/4096 → numerator 1489, denominator 4096\n\nS_13 = 2977/8192 → numerator 2977, denominator 8192\n\nS_14 = 5953/16384 → numerator 5953, denominator 16384\n\nS_15 = 11907/32768 → numerator 11907, denominator 32768\n\nS_16 = 23815/65536 → numerator 23815, denominator 65536\n\nS_17 = 47629/131072 → numerator 47629, denominator 131072\n\nObserving the numerators:\n\n1, 1, 3, 5, 11, 23, 47, 95, 187, 373, 745, 1489, 2977, 5953, 11907, 23815, 47629,...\n\nLooking at the pattern between terms:\n\nFrom 1 to 1: same.\n\