g and converging to around 0.3638...\n\nWait a second, 0.3638 is approximately equal to 1/2.75 or something? Not sure. Alternatively, note that 0.3638 is close to ln(2) ≈0.6931, no, half of that is ~0.3466. Not quite.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps it's 1/√7 ≈0.37796, no. 0.3638 is closer to 1/2.75, but not a nice fraction.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps the exact value is 1/3, but the partial sums are higher. Alternatively, maybe it's 1/2.75? 1/2.75 is 4/11≈0.3636, which is very close to our computed partial sums. Let me check:\n\n4 divided by 11 is approximately 0.363636..., which is very close to the partial sums we're getting (~0.3638). The difference might be due to the remaining terms.\n\nIndeed, 4/11 ≈0.363636..., while our partial sum at n=16 is approximately 0.3638468, so the difference is about 0.00021, which is about 1/5000, so maybe the exact value is 4/11? Or perhaps 13/36 ≈0.3611, which is a bit lower.\n\nAlternatively, let's compute 1489/4096 exactly:\n\n1489 divided by 4096:\n\n4096 goes into 1489 0. times. 1489/4096 = 0.3638671875 exactly.\n\nSimilarly, 2977/8192 = (1489*2 +1)/ (4096*2) = (2978 +1)/8192 =2979/8192 ≈0.3638310547\n\nWait, actually, when we did n=13: 1489/4096 -1/8192 = (2978 -1)/8192 =2977/8192. Yes.\n\nThen n=14: 2977/8192 +1/16384 = (5954 +1)/16384 =5955/16384.\n\n5955/16384 ≈0.3638310547\n\nn=15: 5955/16384 +1/32768 = (11910 +1)/32768 =11911/32768 ≈0.36386165\n\nn=16: 11911/32768 +1/65536 = (23822 +1)/65536 =23823/65536 ≈0.3638468\n\nHmm, so each time we add a positive term, the partial sum increases a little, then when we have a negative term, it decreases.\n\nBut the limit seems to be approaching approximately 0.3638...\n\nWait, let me see what 0.3638 is as a fraction:\n\n0.3638 * 10000 = 3638, so 3638/10000 = 1819/5000 ≈0.3638. But that's not a reduced fraction.\n\nAlternatively, 0.3638 ≈ 1/2.75 = 4/11 ≈0.3636...\n\nAlternatively, 0.3638 is approximately 12/33 ≈0.3636, but 12/33 reduces to 4/11.\n\nAlternatively, 0.3638 is approximately 3