3,4,5, or 6.\n\nSimilarly, from 7, we came from 1, so the other neighbor of 7 is 2, which we already have. Wait, no, in the cycle, 7 is between 1 and 2, so after 2, we have to go to another node that is adjacent to 2 and hasn't been used yet.\n\nLet me attempt to build the cycle step by step, starting at 1, going to 7, then to 2, and then proceeding.\n\nLet me denote the current position and the set of used nodes.\n\nStart at 1 (used: {1}), next to 7 (used: {1,7}), then to 2 (used: {1,7,2}).\n\nFrom 2, the next node must be adjacent to 2 and not yet used. The neighbors of 2 are 1,3,4,5,6,7. But 1 and 7 are already used, so available neighbors are 3,4,5,6.\n\nTherefore, from 2, we can go to 3,4,5, or 6.\n\nLet me consider each possibility separately.\n\nSubcase 1a: From 2, go to 3.\n\nNow the path is 1-7-2-3. Used: {1,7,2,3}\n\nFrom 3, the next node must be adjacent to 3 and not yet used. The neighbors of 3 are 1,2,4,5,6. Used nodes: 1,2,3,7. So available neighbors: 4,5,6.\n\nTherefore, from 3, can go to 4,5, or 6.\n\nSubcase 1a1: 1-7-2-3-4\n\nUsed: {1,7,2,3,4}\n\nFrom 4, neighbors are 1,2,3,5. Used: 1,2,3,4,7. Available: 5.\n\nSo must go to 5.\n\nPath: 1-7-2-3-4-5. Used: {1,2,3,4,5,7}\n\nFrom 5, neighbors are 1,2,3,4. All except 6 are used. Wait, 5 is connected to 1,2,3,4. But 6 is not connected to 5. Wait, 5's neighbors are only up to 4. So from 5, the only unused neighbor is... actually, the only unused node is 6, but 5 is not connected to 6. Therefore, this path is stuck. So this path cannot be extended to a Hamiltonian cycle.\n\nTherefore, Subcase 1a1 is invalid.\n\nSubcase 1a2: 1-7-2-3-5\n\nWait, from 3, instead of going to 4, go to 5.\n\nPath: 1-7-2-3-5. Used: {1,2,3,5,7}\n\nFrom 5, neighbors are 1,2,3,4. Used nodes: 1,2,3,5,7. Available: 4.\n\nSo go to 4.\n\nPath: 1-7-2-3-5-4. Used: {1,2,3,4,5,7}\n\nFrom 4, neighbors are 1,2,3,5. All except 6 are used. The remaining node is 6, but 4 is not connected to 6. Therefore, stuck again. Cannot reach 6.\n\nTherefore, 