 number of B's is T (since B can be 0,1,...,T-1). The number of x-intervals is 15, as before.\n\nTherefore, yes, for each T from 1 to 5, the count is T *15.\n\nTherefore,\n\nS4 = sum_{T=1}^5 [ C(5 - T, 2) * T *15 ]\n\nLet me compute each term:\n\nFirst, note that C(5 - T, 2) is zero when 5 - T < 2, i.e., when T > 3.\n\nSo for T=1,2,3,4,5:\n\nFor T=1:\n\nC(5 -1, 2)=C(4,2)=6\n\nMultiply by T=1: 6*1=6\n\nFor T=2:\n\nC(5-2,2)=C(3,2)=3\n\nMultiply by T=2: 3*2=6\n\nFor T=3:\n\nC(5-3,2)=C(2,2)=1\n\nMultiply by T=3:1*3=3\n\nFor T=4:\n\nC(5-4,2)=C(1,2)=0 (since 1 < 2)\n\nMultiply by T=4:0*4=0\n\nFor T=5:\n\nC(5-5,2)=C(0,2)=0 (since 0 < 2)\n\nMultiply by T=5:0*5=0\n\nTherefore, the terms are:\n\nT=1:6,\n\nT=2:6,\n\nT=3:3,\n\nT=4:0,\n\nT=5:0.\n\nTotal sum inside the brackets:6 +6 +3 +0 +0 =15\n\nTherefore, S4 =15 *15=225.\n\nWait, hold on, no:\n\nWait, actually, the terms above are already multiplied by T and C(5-T,2). Wait, let me recast:\n\nWait, S4 = sum_{T=1}^5 [ C(5 - T, 2) * T *15 ]\n\nSo, for each T, compute C(5-T,2)*T, then multiply by 15, then sum over T.\n\nWait, no, actually, the 15 is already factored in. Wait, no:\n\nWait, no, actually, in my previous step:\n\nWait, I think I messed up the factors.\n\nWait, S4 = sum_{T=1}^5 [ C(5 - T, 2) * (number of rectangles with top T) ]\n\nBut the number of rectangles with top T is T *15, so:\n\nS4 = sum_{T=1}^5 [ C(5 - T, 2) * (T *15) ]\n\nTherefore, the total is 15 * sum_{T=1}^5 [ C(5 - T, 2) * T ]\n\nTherefore, compute the inner sum first:\n\nsum_{T=1}^5 [ C(5 - T, 2) * T ]\n\nLet me compute term by term:\n\nFor T=1:\n\nC(4,2)*1 =6*1=6\n\nT=2:\n\nC(3,2)*2=3*2=6\n\nT=3:\n\nC(2,2)*3=1*3=3\n\nT=4:\n\nC(1,2)*4=0*4=0\n\nT=5:\n\nC(0,2)*5=0*5=0\n\nSo sum is 6+6+3+0+0=15\n\nTherefore, S4 =15 *15=225.\n\nTherefore, S4 =225.\n\nTherefore, putting it all together:\n\nS = S1 + S2 + S3 + S4 = 225 +75 +225 +225.\n\nLet me compute that:\n\n225 +75 = 300,\n\n300 +225 =525,\n\n525 +225=750.\n\nTherefore, S =750.\n\nTherefore, going back to